   "what_it_did": "Until its first reply arrived (step 33, 1.65 s) the runtime held every joint, the grippers included, at its measured position, so the sticks sat in the fingers at under 1 N (not held by the hit rule); nothing touched a pad. Its first reply closed both grippers (27 to 33 N, both sticks held from step 34); from about step 49 it opened both grippers wide, and both sticks fell onto their pads (left on the hi-hat, right on the snare) at 2.7 s. The right gripper took the right stick again twice (steps 134 to 214 and 582 to 744), the left gripper the left stick only for a moment (near 13.8 s), and touched the snare with it 21 times, none faster than 0.19 m/s, so none was a hit (a hit needs 0.5 m/s). The four contacts at 0.5 m/s or more were all by sticks that were not held (2.7 s on the snare and the hi-hat, 53.7 and 53.8 s on the snare's rim). The left stick ended on the table beside the left arm's base, the right one loose on the snare. No gripper or arm touched a pad; 0 of 41 notes, no tempo fitted, so the score was 0 throughout.",
